1. Execution Restrictions

AI must not execute or apply changes automatically without explicit confirmation from the developer.

All code modifications must be proposed first and applied only after developer approval.

2. Documentation Language

All documentation, summaries, comments, and code explanations must be written strictly in English.

No other languages are allowed in:

code comments
summaries
documentation blocks
guidelines
3. Modification Scope

AI must not modify classes that are not explicitly provided in the request.

Allowed modifications:

Only the classes, methods, or files explicitly included in the developer's message.

Forbidden:

Editing unrelated files
Editing external services
Editing infrastructure classes
Editing models not included in the request
4. Refactoring Restrictions

During refactoring AI must not change existing program logic.

Allowed:

formatting
code readability improvements
naming improvements
documentation additions

Forbidden:

behavioral changes
altering execution flow
modifying conditions or algorithms
changing method responsibilities
5. API Integrity

AI must not replace or alter existing APIs.

Forbidden actions:

replacing existing services with alternative implementations
introducing new frameworks or libraries without request
changing method signatures
changing return types
altering service contracts
6. Logical Error Reporting

If AI detects potential logical errors or risky behavior during review, it must:

Notify the developer
Explain the issue
Not modify the logic automatically

All fixes must be approved by the developer before implementation.

7. Architecture Preservation

AI must respect the existing architecture:

AvaloniaUI
Model–View–ViewModel

Forbidden:

breaking MVVM boundaries
moving business logic to Views
creating UI elements directly inside ViewModels
8. Service Access Rules

Services must be accessed only through the project DI container.

Allowed methods:

[Inject] attribute
Di.Container.GetInstance<T>()
Di.Container.ResolveFieldsFromClassInstance(this)

Direct creation of services using new is not allowed.

9. Database Rules

All database operations must go through DatabaseService.

Forbidden:

direct DbContext usage inside ViewModels
direct SQL queries inside ViewModels
bypassing the database service layer
10. Safety Principle

When uncertain about the impact of a change, AI must:

Stop
Ask the developer for clarification
Avoid making assumptions.

No speculative modifications are allowed.